SUMMARY:Fladder v0.11.1
DESCRIPTION:Fladder 0.11.1 | Fladder-iOS-0.11.1\n\n<!-- Release notes gener
 ated using configuration in .github/release.yml at v0.11.1 -->\n\n## What'
 s Changed\nRelease is v0.11.1 is a hot-fix release for v0.11.0 mainly fixi
 ng local network connections not working on Android. Besides that the chan
 gelog remains the same.\n\n## Music playback\n\nMusic playback has finally
  arrived after a long time.\n\n<img height="480" alt="music_dashboard" src
 ="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a5f829d2-bd65-4502-b06f-7c55b
 f465b58" />\n\nThe music dashboard can be accessed by long pressing the ho
 me button and selecting music dashboard.\n\nIncluding the following featur
 es\n- Music dashboard\n- Gapless playback\n- Volume normalization\n- Fade 
 in/out when pausing and switching tracks that are not in the same album\n-
  Lyrics\n- Syncing of playlist albums tracks etc.\n\nThe music playback is
  probably best considered to be in beta. While everything works there can 
 and will be small bugs/annoyances. For AndroidTV navigation of the player 
 controls are a bit cumbersome and will be improved along with other dPad i
 mprovements\n\n## Picture-in-Picture\n<img  height="480" alt="pip" src="ht
 tps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b808c9b7-c4f2-43e4-9f4d-3bcab96b9
 f36" />\n\n## Filters 2.0 + Library search improvements\nThe filters in th
 e library search view have now been improved. Besides a lot of small bugfi
 xes\, more settings are now saved. \n- Allow setting filters for specific 
 folders inside libraries not just libraries themselves\n- Add any saved fi
 lter to the side navigation bar\n- Setting a "default/favorite" filter tha
 t applies instead of the default behavior for that library.\n\n## Ambient 
 blur\nFor the people that don't like black-bars around their videos there 
 is now the option to enable "ambient blur" this generates a YouTube "theat
 her" like blur around videos.\n\n##\n\n### Exciting New Features 🏕\n* f
 eat: Add hotkeys to step through frames by @peanut250 in https://github.co
 m/DonutWare/Fladder/pull/928\n* feat: Add hotkeys for inst
URL:https://raynmahbub.github.io/OmniSource/feeds/fladder.json
